From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:41:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 23/25] [Core] Honor --prefill-schedule-interval without data
 parallelism

--prefill-schedule-interval N defers prefill work to one engine step in
N while other requests decode, but only the DP engine core implements
the throttle; the base EngineCore never throttles, so the flag does
nothing on a single-engine deployment. There a long chunked prefill
shares every step with the running decodes, and on GB10 a 32k prefill
holds the decoders to ~1 tok/s.

Implement the base throttle from the scheduler's own step counter, read
before schedule() advances it. The scheduler's existing gates still
apply: prefills run anyway when nothing is decoding or the batch is
capacity bound (prefill_capacity_bound). The default interval of 1
changes nothing.

Source: knapcio/GLM-5.3-Flash-4x-DGX-Spark-TP4 @ 770d115,
  overlay/glm_prefill_sched.py, E27 cadence (MIT), which credits
  jnardiello's GLM-5.3-Flash-FP8-4-DGX-Spark-Switchless E27 (MIT) and
  FujitsuPolycom's SparkRing non-DP EngineCore._should_throttle_prefills.
  Re-implemented here in three lines. Not ported: E27b short-prefill
  bypass, E27c cadence while requests are queued, E29 end-drain hold
  and idle coalescing (scheduler-internal source edits).
Upstream: absent in v0.31.0 and main. #57951 and #58459 (both in
  v0.31.0) only change the long_prefill_token_threshold cap, not the
  cadence.
Claimed gain: knapcio (4x GB10, TP=4, cadence 8 together with E27b/c and
  E29): decoders under a 32k prefill 1.3 -> 7.3 tok/s, "short newcomer
  at c4 -22%", TTFT -8%, step time unchanged. Opt-in: set
  --prefill-schedule-interval 8.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vllm/config/scheduler.py |  7 ++++---
 vllm/v1/engine/core.py   | 15 ++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/config/scheduler.py b/vllm/config/scheduler.py
index 1fb94d3ef..e83683568 100644
--- a/vllm/config/scheduler.py
+++ b/vllm/config/scheduler.py
@@ -202,9 +202,10 @@ class SchedulerConfig:
     (the default) disables the watermark."""
 
     prefill_schedule_interval: int = Field(default=1, ge=1)
-    """For data-parallel deployments, only admit new prefill requests
-    once every N engine steps, aligned across DP ranks, to better balance
-    per-step forward-pass times."""
+    """Only schedule prefill work once every N engine steps while other
+    requests are decoding. With data parallelism the steps are aligned across
+    DP ranks, to better balance per-step forward-pass times; without it, this
+    keeps long prefills from stalling every decode step."""
 
     async_scheduling: bool | None = None
     """If set to False, disable async scheduling. Async scheduling helps to
diff --git a/vllm/v1/engine/core.py b/vllm/v1/engine/core.py
index 5c09a0059..25a7baa3c 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/engine/core.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/engine/core.py
@@ -623,9 +623,18 @@ class EngineCore:
             eco.scheduler_stats.iteration_details = iteration_details
 
     def _should_throttle_prefills(self) -> bool:
-        """Whether to defer new prefills this step (DP prefill balancing).
-        Overridden by the DP engine core; never throttles otherwise."""
-        return False
+        """Whether to defer prefill work this step.
+
+        With --prefill-schedule-interval N > 1, prefills run on one step in N
+        while other requests decode, so a long prefill does not stall every
+        decode step. The scheduler still admits them when nothing decodes or
+        it is capacity bound. The DP engine core overrides this with a step
+        counter aligned across DP ranks.
+        """
+        interval = self.vllm_config.scheduler_config.prefill_schedule_interval
+        # Before schedule() advances it; plugin schedulers may not count steps.
+        step = getattr(self.scheduler, "current_step", 0)
+        return interval > 1 and step % interval != 0
 
     def step(self) -> tuple[dict[int, EngineCoreOutputs], bool]:
         """Schedule, execute, and make output.
